{
  "family": "A_calibration",
  "description": "Locate the measured WAL ceiling on THIS hardware. Levels 1-6 sweep commit rate at one row per commit, which characterises the low-volume regime and finds the commit-rate ceiling. Levels 7-10 remove the rate limit entirely and raise batch size, which is what actually pushes bytes hard enough to reach the apply-capacity ceiling - a commit-rate sweep alone tops out around 10 MB/s and would never find it. Read the highest measured_wal_mb_per_sec where exceeded_capacity is still false, and retarget matrices B-F from it.",
